obal economic history. The book’s strength lies in its clear explanations of complex theories – particularly the link between high wages and technological innovation – with one reader finding it surprisingly insightful even with a background in finance and economics. The narrative receives mixed reactions, with some finding its fast-paced, fact-based approach invigorating while others wished for more detailed transitions between topics; however, most agree it offers a valuable overview of the forces shaping global prosperity and inequality over the last 500 years. Ultimately, customers consider it suitable for anyone wanting a broad understanding of economic development and its relevance to current events.\n\n## Reader reviews\n\n4.0 Average\n\n1 - 5 of 10 reviews\n\nVery Good\n\nbooktsunami\n\nMar 14, 2024\n\nPartner review\n\nWell, What would you expect from a book that promises it is a very short introduction to a very complex subject? --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGlobal Economic History: A Very Short Introduction by Robert C. Allen: Compare Prices on New & Used Copies | ISBN: 0198921837 - Alibris (https://www.alibris.com/search/books/isbn/0198921837)\nciteturn2search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; \n$9.19, new condition, Sold by Ingram Customer Returns Center rated 5.0 out of 5 stars, ships from NV, USA, published 2026 by Oxford University Press.\nImage: Global Economic History: A Very Short Introduction\n    * Edition:\n    * 2026, Oxford University Press\n    * Paperback, New\n    * Available Copies: 10+\n    * Details:\n    * ISBN: 0198921837\n    * ISBN-13: 9780198921837\n    * Publisher: Oxford University Press\n    * Published: 2026\n    * Language: English\n    * New. Contains: Unspecified. Very Short Introductions . Includes unspecified. Intended for college/higher education audience.\n    * ► Contact This Seller\nHide Details ▴\n  * Paperback, Fine/Like New 2026, O